From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:33:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(dp): XRT_DP_SCANOUT_FLAG_FULL_SIDE_BY_SIDE, an
 output for a stereo compositor

A display processor whose output is the views placed side by side, view 0
(the left eye) first, each at the resolution its tile was rendered at, hands
the desktop a picture a stereo compositor can show per eye: the layout HDMI
1.4b calls 3D structure "Side-by-Side (Full)". The runtime cannot infer that
from the pixels, so the DP says it, per instance and per mode, with a new bit
in the existing xrt_dp_scanout_caps::flags word (no layout change, no ABI
bump: a plug-in built before the bit wrote 0 there, an ordinary weave).

xrt_display_processor_vk_outputs_full_sbs() reads it with the same
"didn't answer means no" rule as the resample bit, and the unit test pins the
back-compat gate: a plug-in built before get_scanout_caps is never called, a
NULL slot or a declining DP reads no, and only the bit itself says yes.

